meta {
  name: VC - File Upload - Stream Response
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/vc?response_mode=stream
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  response_mode: stream
}

body:multipart-form {
  input_audio: @file(./test-files/sample-recording.wav)
  target_voice_source: test_voices/linda_johnson_02.mp3
  chunk_sec: 60
  overlap_sec: 0.1
  export_formats: wav,mp3
  disable_watermark: true
}

docs {
  # Voice Conversion - File Upload with Streaming Response
  
  Upload audio files directly without pre-staging them on the server.
  
  ## Input Method
  - **Content-Type**: multipart/form-data
  - **File Upload**: Direct upload in the request (max 100MB)
  - **Target Voice**: Still references file in reference_audio/
  
  ## Form Fields
  - **input_audio**: File upload field (required)
  - **target_voice_source**: Target voice filename (required)
  - **chunk_sec**: Integer, default 60
  - **overlap_sec**: Float, default 0.1
  - **export_formats**: Comma-separated string (e.g., "wav,mp3,flac")
  - **disable_watermark**: Boolean, default true
  
  ## Response
  - Binary audio file streamed directly
  - Content-Type matches the requested format
  - Content-Disposition with generated filename
  - X-Alternative-Formats lists other generated files
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Web interfaces with file upload forms
  - Mobile apps recording and converting audio
  - Client applications without server access
  - Processing user-uploaded content
  
  ## File Requirements
  - Maximum file size: 100MB
  - Supported formats: WAV, MP3, FLAC
  - Recommended: Clear speech, minimal noise
  
  ## Note on Test File
  Replace `@file(./test-files/sample-recording.wav)` with an actual file path
  relative to this Bruno collection or use an absolute path.
}
